BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Romance vs Reality of Entrepreneurship
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6aaad5c6ca248a00291644a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\n“The only thing that prepares you to run a bus
 iness is running a business.” – Ben Horowitz.\nWhat is an entrepreneur
 ? One of many lessons learned from Jean’s fourteen-year journey as a pas
 sionate food entrepreneur and her ongoing fifteen-year small business coac
 hing practice is that “entrepreneur” is not a job title. Join us for t
 he first session of Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcome Focus)\, Jean Chow'
 s\, residency at the Fort York branch!\nThis session will include:\nSelf-a
 ssessment – “Should I Be An Entrepreneur?”\nReflection on your curre
 nt passion level.\nBalancing the risks associated with entrepreneurial pas
 sion.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-on-one consu
 ltations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please fill out the in-ta
 ke form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad5c6ca248a00291644a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
