BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T150000
UID:698bcc69cbf1533ca536cacf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 Yellowface\nby R. F. Kuang.\nAfter witnessing the death of literary star A
 thena Liu\, June Hayward acts on impulse: she steals Athena's masterpiece 
 and claims it as her own. Rebranded as the elusive "Juniper Song\," June m
 ust navigate a minefield of social media scrutiny and looming exposure in 
 this dark thriller about literary theft and identity.\nPick up a physical 
 copy at the branch before the meeting\, or find copies through our website
  in various formats. Registration is required and begins Aug. 27\, 2026.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcc69cbf1533ca536cacf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
