BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food Justice in Toronto: Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6ac3e146a85a2c00337d59a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join an expert-led discussion on food justice in your communit
 y. Learn about Toronto's food system\, the issues that affect our food acc
 ess\, and discover strategies to address food insecurity and inequity. The
  panel will be followed by a facilitated group discussion reflecting on en
 gagement with local food systems and practices.\nPanelists include:\nShath
  Ramesh\n(she/they) is a community organizer and the Urban Agriculture Coo
 rdinator at Malvern Family Resource Centre\, where they manage the Malvern
  Urban Farmers' Market. They hold a Masters in sustainability studies from
  Trent University and are passionate about food justice\, climate action a
 nd advocacy.\nJade Guthrie\n(she/her) is a queer\, mixed-race educator\, 
 facilitator\, and community organizer. As the Manager of Community Learnin
 g and Engagement at FoodShare Toronto\, jade is committed to social change
  work rooted in justice\, liberation\, and joy and approaches this work wi
 th tenderness\, curiosity\, and reciprocity. Beyond 9-5\, jade is an organ
 izer with Justicia for Migrant Workers\, a board member at Food Secure Can
 ada\, and sits on the City of Toronto’s Black Food Sovereignty Action Pl
 an Advisory Circle.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
