DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
UID:6a96f236aafa61002960b336@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) presentation will cover tax o
 bligations for small business owners of incorporated businesses.\nA CRA Li
 aison Officer will cover:\n- Business tax deductions\n- Common tax errors\
 n- Helpful tools and services offered by the CRA\n- General bookkeeping co
 ncepts and best practices\n***\nThis 2-hour program is held online via CRA
 's MS Teams. Please register to receive information on how to attend (an
  event reminder email will be sent approximately 24 hours before the ev
 ent begins).\nThis program will not be recorded. Captions will be availabl
 e.\n***\nAdditional CRA Info Sessions\nWe also offer an additional CRA Ta
 x Information Session for Small Corporations (T2) on\nTuesday\, October 20
 \, 2026 - 6:30 to 8:30 pm\n.\nLooking for a CRA info session for unincorpo
 rated small business owners and self-employed individuals (T1)? We also of
 fer them on:\nTuesday\, October 13\, 2026 - 6:30 to 8:30 pm\nThursday\, Oc
 tober 15\, 2026 - 12:00 to 2:00 pm\nNeed help with MS Teams?\nJoining a T
 eams Meeting\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f236aafa61002960b336
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6aaea67bf9ed2e003851e601@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 4: E-COMMERCE\, SECURE PAYMENTS & LAUNCH\nIn this final\, pi
 votal session\, we transform the websites into fully functional online sto
 res. We will cover\nthe comprehensive setup of WooCommerce\, including pro
 duct listing and category management\, with\na major focus on Stripe payme
 nt integration for secure transactions. The session concludes with a final
 \nsite review\, troubleshooting\, and a collaborative Q&A to ensure each p
 articipant feels confident\nmanaging and growing their new online store.\n
 KEYWORDS: WOOCOMMERCE SETUP · PRODUCT LISTING · STRIPE PAYMENT INTEGRATI
 ON · SITE\nREVIEW · Q&A\nLearners who complete all the courses will earn
  a certificate of completion.\n(\nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nPlea
 se cancel as soon as possible if you are no longer available to attend\n.)
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaea67bf9ed2e003851e601
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 3
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T200000
UID:6aaea5f8f9ed2e003851e5e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 3: NAVIGATION\, UX & CONTACT INTEGRATION\nThe third session 
 is dedicated to building a seamless and intuitive user journey. We will di
 ve into\ncreating effective navigation menus and professional footers whil
 e utilizing the Elementor page\nbuilder to design functional sub-pages. We
  will also implement professional contact forms and\nintegrate lead genera
 tion tools with participants' email systems\, ensuring visitors can easily
  find\ninformation and connect with the business across all devices.\nKEYW
 ORDS: NAVIGATION MENUS · ELEMENTOR PAGE BUILDER · SUB-PAGES · CONTACT F
 ORMS ·\nLEAD GENERATION\nLearners who complete all the courses will earn 
 a certificate of completion.\n(\nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nPleas
 e cancel as soon as possible if you are no longer available to attend\n.)\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaea5f8f9ed2e003851e5e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
