DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T150000
UID:6a750fecf4e5db3d00c6fe8e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Palmerston branch and its neighbourhood is home to a varie
 ty of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nto explore th
 e natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize diff
 erent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance
 .\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nPlease re
 gister. Space is limited.\nThe tour will start and end outside of the Palm
 erston Library and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry s
 taff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress
  and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, h
 ats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rai
 n or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be
  notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Frag
 ile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Librar
 y\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Main Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a750fecf4e5db3d00c6fe8e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
