BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 and 2 Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T153000
UID:6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5d0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Tuesday afternoons from Septemb
 er 22 to December 8\, 2-3:30pm. Learning circles are study groups guided b
 y staff for people who want to take a free online course together in a wel
 coming space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course ma
 terials. Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course
  and attend all learning circle sessions.\nLearners who successfully compl
 ete both courses will earn a digital badge and certificate of completion.\
 nPython Essentials 1\nis the first in a 2-course series that teaches compu
 ter programming skills including how to design\, develop\, and improve com
 puter programs using the Python programming language. The course covers es
 sential programming topics such as data types\, variables\, control flow\,
  functions\, and exceptions.\nPython Essentials 2\nis the second in a 2-co
 urse series that will prepare you for the PCAP – Certified Associate in 
 Python Programming certification exam at Pearson VUE. This intermediate-le
 vel course covers advanced aspects of Python programming\, including modul
 es\, packages\, exceptions\, file processing and object-oriented programmi
 ng (OOP).\nFor more information about the Python learning circle\, please 
 contact\nnetworkingacademy@tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:York Woods
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5d0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Three “Know’s for Success as an Entrepreneur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T200000
UID:6aaad5e3ab7a8e0037c24145@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service\nIn this highly interactive workshop with Entrepre
 neur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, we’ll explore how well 
 you know yourself\, know your reason why you want to own a business\, and 
 will your customers need and want to buy what you are offering. What are t
 he key traits of an entrepreneur? Is this an opportunity worth pursuing\, 
 a T.R.U.E. (Testable\, Real. Unique\, Essential) value proposition? Who ar
 e your customers?\nThis session will include:\nKnow your dominant dimensio
 n as an entrepreneur – “heart\, smarts\, guts\, or luck”.\nPinpoint 
 your “why” with your T.R.U.E. value proposition and articulate the pro
 blem you are solving. Is it an opportunity worth pursuing?\nCreate a buyer
  persona/ideal customer profile (ICP) to demonstrate how well you know you
 r target audience.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one
 -on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please fill 
 out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad5e3ab7a8e0037c24145
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T160000
UID:6aa45f49101eb7003f2f5ede@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nAttend all four sessions in person at\nBarbara Frum Branc
 h on October 9\, 16\, 23\, 30 from 2-4pm.\nRegistration is a two-step proc
 edure. First\, participants must complete their registration through this 
 page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to request additional
  information in order to complete the registration.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Program Room on 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa45f49101eb7003f2f5ede
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ageing In Place: How To Assess Your Long Term Care Options
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
UID:6ab1ba6b129d8e0031f41d0f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Where do you want to spend your retirement years and how can y
 ou make that happen?\nLooking ahead and having a plan gives us control. Ra
 ther than leaving things up to chance\, we get to make the choices and dec
 isions that we want--not that someone else wants. Karen Henderson\, an ex
 pert in long term care options\, shares her knowledge and resources to hel
 p you make more informed decisions.\nAs the result of a life changing 14-y
 ear dementia care experience\, Karen founded the Long Term Care Planning N
 etwork\, Canada’s leading resource centre for ageing\, eldercare and lon
 g term care planning and education. Her seminar series\, web site and prin
 t/electronic tools are recognized as key long term care educational resour
 ces for Canadian families.\nKaren is a Certified Professional Consultant o
 n Aging (CPCA).
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab1ba6b129d8e0031f41d0f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
