BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lessons from Home to “Here”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6aaad6f9ca248a002916457f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nA panel of newcomer professionals\, moderated b
 y Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, will share the
 ir successful journey from their life at “home” to their new home. Wha
 t are their lessons learned as newcomer entrepreneurs where they can now g
 ive back to their new home and community?\nIn this session:\nBe inspired b
 y established newcomer entrepreneurs.\nGain motivation to work on your bus
 iness and not in your business.\nUnderstand and overcome barriers unique t
 o newcomer entrepreneurs\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply f
 or one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, please
  fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad6f9ca248a002916457f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
