BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T200000
UID:6a51496188e9bf28002ff5e8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nFri
 day\, October 2\, 5pm-7pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a 
 week for 8 weeks\, October 9 - November 27\n. Registration closes after we
 ek 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and ref
 reshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Cr
 isis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsi
 ble for the protection of \npersonal information collected through the pro
 gram registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a51496188e9bf28002ff5e8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Austen & Company Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T160000
UID:694432a26724c63d00e78fef@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Formerly known as Cedarbrae’s Jane Austen Book Club\, we now
  invite you to meet us monthly to discuss works from the 18th-20th centuri
 es\, books about those works and their authors\, and re-tellings and books
  inspired by them. Ask to borrow print copies at the branch or borrow digi
 tal versions online from Libby or Hoopla.\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae - Closed\, FCCR on main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/694432a26724c63d00e78fef
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reschedule: Small Business Health & Safety Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T190000
UID:6a551594dee4ff5300c931d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As a small business owner\, you have legal obligations when it
  comes to the health and safety of your\nworkplace. But it's not just abou
 t the law. A sound workplace health and safety program will also ensure\nt
 he growth of your business.\n\nDon’t know how to start? This presentatio
 n will guide you through the journey.\n\nWhat you will learn:\n• Who are
  Workplace Safety & Prevention Services (WSPS)?\n• What is the occupatio
 nal health and safety system in Ontario?\n• What is the Occupation Healt
 h & Safety Act (OHSA)?\n• What are responsibilities of the employer\, th
 e supervisor\, and the worker in health & safety?\n• How can I use WSPS 
 Small Business Centre?\n• What other free resources does WSPS provide?\n
 • What is WSIB’s Health & Safety Excellence program (HSEp)?\n\nPlease 
 note: This is a rescheduled program for Wednesday\, October 28\, 2026. The
  new date is Wednesday\, November 4\, 2026.\n\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a551594dee4ff5300c931d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6a987af8e1fb8f13578ba603@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free\, culturally affirming drop-in program for adults that 
 promotes mental wellness through creative activities\, discussion\, and he
 althy coping strategies. Guided by the concept of Sankofa\, participants e
 xplore connections between past experiences and present wellbeing while bu
 ilding skills for managing stress and supporting mental health. Activities
  vary based on community interests and needs.\nThis program is in collabor
 ation with\nTAIBU Community Health Centre\n.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a987af8e1fb8f13578ba603
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee and Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T150000
UID:695d7436f21d1d99bcda1b38@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and informal discussion about 
 services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and le
 t us know what information and resources you would like to access at the l
 ibrary and in the community.\nEach month we will be joined by a different 
 community organization. Upcoming guests at Lillian H. Smith branch:\nFrida
 y\, September 25\n:\nTPL staff (Indigenous Initiatives) and WoodGreen\nFri
 day\, October 23*:\nVolunteer T.O.\nFriday\, November 27:\nOsteoporosis Ca
 nada\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredien
 t lists will be available at the program.\n*Please note the date change (p
 reviously October 30)
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695d7436f21d1d99bcda1b38
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
