END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Launch Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6ab6d22565abe8002a7c147d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThe 8-week program closes with a networki
 ng-focused workshop where participants pitch their one-page plan to peers 
 and invited community partners. The session explores how to build a person
 al board of advisors made up of mentors\, peers\, and champions. Participa
 nts leave with clear next steps\, including one-on-one consultations\, ong
 oing supports\, and ways to stay connected with the community they have bu
 ilt.\nDrop-in\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident ent
 repreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/ei
 r\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until availab
 le slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d22565abe8002a7c147d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Selling with Confidence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
UID:6ab6d13e65abe8002a7c13ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThis practice-based workshop covers the f
 undamentals of selling: listening well\, communicating value\, and followi
 ng up. Participants learn to handle pricing conversations and respond to t
 he common "it's too expensive" objection. Through roleplay\, each particip
 ant practices a 60-second pitch of their business live\, with coaching on 
 the spot.\nDrop-In\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our residen
 t entrepreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.
 ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until av
 ailable slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d13e65abe8002a7c13ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Navigating Essential Financial Tools for Beginner & Newcomer Entre
 preneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T200000
UID:6a886432392e9c02993c056a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Navigating self-employment in a new country can be challenging
 \, but this workshop will equip newly immigrated entrepreneurs (and new en
 trepreneurs in general) with the essential financial tools to succeed in 
 Canada. This workshop is designed to build your confidence in managing you
 r business finances and help you thrive as a self-employed professional in
  Canada. Perfect for newcomers looking to establish a solid financial foun
 dation.​\nRegistration required.\nInformation Collection Notice: The per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a886432392e9c02993c056a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibit Tour of Set Phasers to Celebrate! 60 Years of Star Trek: A
  Merril Collection Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T190000
UID:6a89a314aafa6100295e52b6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of our current exhibit\,\nSet Phaser
 s to Celebrate! 60 Years of Star Trek: A Merril Collection Exhibit\n!\nThi
 s exhibit looks at one of the most beloved and influential science fictio
 n franchises of all time. Star Trek has been boldly exploring brave new wo
 rlds and new frontiers for 60 years. Explore the history of the franchise 
 with our knowledgeable staff. The tour will also cover topics like the r
 ise of fan culture\, the campaign to Save Star Trek from cancellation and
  much more.\nCome celebrate the 60th anniversary of Star Trek with us!\nTh
 is will be a half-hour tour\, followed by time to ask questions and explor
 e the exhibit.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a89a314aafa6100295e52b6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
