BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet the Winner of the 2026 Giller Prize
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T190000
UID:6a85b35736204e08fbb58141@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The winner of the 2026 Giller Prize will join us to discuss th
 eir winning work — who will it be?\nThe to-be-announced winner will be i
 n conversation with journalist Mark Medley.\nQ&A and book signing to follo
 w. Books available for purchase.\n***\nMeet the Finalists:\n2026 Giller Pr
 ize Shortlist\nThe authors on the 2026 Giller Prize shortlist are:\nTara G
 ereaux\nfor her novel\nWild People Quiet\n\, published by Scribner Canada\
 nMichelle Good\nfor her novel\nEliza Sunshine\n\, published by Random Hous
 e Canada\nNicholas Herring\nfor his novel\nYour Breath in Charcoal\n\, pub
 lished by Goose Lane Editions\nNazanine Hozar\nfor her novel\nThe Small On
 es\n\, published by Knopf Canada\nPatmeena Sabit\nfor her novel\nGood Peop
 le\n\, published by Crown\n***\nAbout this event’s guests:\nMark Medley\
 n***\nPlease note that this event starts at 6:00pm.\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:
 \nLocation:\nJack Rabinovitch Reading Room\, Toronto Reference Library (78
 9 Yonge Street)\, 4th floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00p
 m.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell the
 se events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity
  to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. 
 Seating first come\, first served\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to acc
 essibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request
  accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca o
 r 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
