DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T153000
UID:6aac2d30129d8e0031f304c3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Learning Centre - Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac2d30129d8e0031f304c3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
