BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T203000
UID:6ac7b588686221156abba69d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\,\nThursdays Nov. 5\, 12\, 19 and 26 from 6-8:30pm.\nRegi
 stration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete their r
 egistration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow
  up to request additional information in order to complete the registratio
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7b588686221156abba69d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Diabetes Myths and Facts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T130000
UID:6ac6a3499d27a000454f55a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Living with diabetes or prediabetes can come with a lot of inf
 ormation about what to eat\, what to avoid\, and how to manage your blood 
 sugar. With so much advice out there\, it can be difficult to separate fac
 t from fiction or know where to focus.\nJoin Catherine Cai\, Registered Di
 etitian and Certified Diabetes Educator\, for a practical and interactive 
 session that separates fact from fiction and explores realistic ways to be
 tter understand and manage diabetes and prediabetes.\nWhat to Expect\nUnde
 rstanding Blood Sugar:\nLearn what your levels mean and how an A1C test pr
 ovides a picture of your average levels over time.\nDiabetes Myths and Fac
 ts:\nExplore common myths      and misconceptions about diabetes and separ
 ate fact from fiction.\nLifestyle and Blood Sugar:\nLearn how sleep\,     
  stress and other lifestyle factors can affect blood sugar.\nBuilding Bala
 nced Meals:\nLearn practical ways      to build balanced\, diabetes-friend
 ly meals.\nBalance\, Not Perfection:\nExplore how balance      and consist
 ency can support diabetes management without striving for      perfection.
 \nAbout the Presenter\nCatherine Cai is a Registered Dietitian and Certifi
 ed Diabetes Educator at Crosstown Family Health Team. She provides practic
 al information and guidance to help people better understand nutrition and
  support their health.\nThis program is presented by Toronto Public Librar
 y in collaboration with the West Toronto Ontario Health Team (OHT)\, a net
 work of over 40 local health and social service providers working together
  to improve the health and well-being of communities in West Toronto.\nYou
 r Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour
  Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted health programs and res
 ources to help people make informed decisions about their health. Learn mo
 re by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nReserve Your Spot To
 day!\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join but registration is required
 . Once registered\, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nWe can
 ’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac6a3499d27a000454f55a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
