BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeff Chang: Bruce Lee and the Making of Asian America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6a85b7fa1401fd00606cea3c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents award-winning author Jeff Chang in conversation w
 ith [HOST TBC] at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Salon\, celebratin
 g what would have been Bruce Lee's birthday.\nMore than half a century aft
 er his death\, Bruce Lee remains as towering a figure as ever\, the man wh
 o popularized martial arts in the West\, became a bridge between Eastern a
 nd Western culture\, and was poised to conquer Hollywood when he died sudd
 enly at age thirty-two. But in the decades since\, his legend has eclipsed
  the man. Forgotten is the immigrant\, the fighter\, the seeker\, the teac
 her\, the father grappling with exile and belonging in a country that ques
 tioned his right to simply exist.\nIn his epic new cultural biography\nWat
 er Mirror Echo: Bruce Lee and the Making of Asian America\n\, acclaimed au
 thor Jeff Chang recovers the man behind the icon. Drawing on in-depth inte
 rviews with Lee's closest intimates\, thousands of newly available persona
 l documents\, and dozens of rare photographs from the family archive\, Cha
 ng traces Lee's remarkable journey: a charismatic child star turned delinq
 uent teen fighter in Hong Kong\, exiled alone to America\, who transformed
  personal struggle into a philosophy of movement and being. Chang reveals 
 how Lee's rise didn't just create a Hollywood legend\, it helped birth som
 ething even more enduring: the very concept of Asian America.\nJoin Jeff C
 hang for a special evening honoring Bruce Lee's birthday\, offering a stir
 ringly human portrait of the icon\, the immigrant\, and the movement he un
 knowingly ignited.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for pu
 rchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nJeff Chang\nRead more:\nWater Mirro
 r Echo\nCan't Stop Won't Stop\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and 
 Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd flo
 or\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree regist
 ration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that 
 the greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guara
 nteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, firs
 t served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\nA
 ccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have 
 a disability and would like to request accommodation for this event\, plea
 se contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks 
 prior to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Serie
 s\n\, where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers
  in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\nThis event is also 
 part of TPL's\nAsian Heritage\nSeries.\nPresenting Sponsor of Heritage Pro
 grams: TD Bank Group\, through the TD Ready Commitment.\n***\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted t
 o fill out a brief survey following the program. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at ans
 werline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b7fa1401fd00606cea3c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marlon James: The Disappearers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6a85b7bd2f41840bbfc30784@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents Booker Prize-winning author Marlon James in conve
 rsation with Kamal Al-Solaylee at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Sa
 lon.\nIn his triumphant return to the Jamaica of his Booker Prize-winning\
 nA Brief History of Seven Killings\n\, Marlon James delivers\nThe Disappea
 rers\n\, an epic\, unflinching novel about survival in the aftermath of vi
 olence. Written with the language-rich\, urgent style that has made James 
 one of the most acclaimed novelists working today\, this is a story of men
  forced to make impossible compromises to survive a society that demands t
 heir erasure.\nAt once a detective story and a searing sociocultural histo
 ry\,\nThe Disappearers\nplunges into the tragic\, ongoing consequences of 
 violent homophobia\, rendering its characters' inner lives with the vivid 
 imagery\, sharp dialogue\, and unrelenting energy that have defined James'
 s celebrated body of work.\nJoin one of the most acclaimed novelists of hi
 s generation\, in conversation with Kamal Al-Solaylee\, for an evening exp
 loring rage\, resilience\, and the price of queer solidarity in a world bu
 ilt to deny it.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purch
 ase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nMarlon James\nKamal Al-Solaylee\nRead 
 more:\nThe Disappearers\nA Brief History of Seven Killings\nReturn\n***\nP
 LAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference
  Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event 
 starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe 
 oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an
  opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity 
 is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available
  for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to ac
 cessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to reques
 t accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca 
 or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event 
 is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and interna
 tional authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about their new book
 s and big ideas.\nThis event is also part of TPL's\nBlack History and Cult
 ure\nSeries.\nPresenting Sponsor of Heritage Programs: TD Bank Group\, thr
 ough the TD Ready Commitment.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey 
 following the program. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b7bd2f41840bbfc30784
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
