BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connect 4: A Conversation Workshop with GenWell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T190000
UID:6ac69b53295b3b0033cadd08@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Connect4 Workshop with GenWell\nA playful\, no-pressure challe
 nge that turns strangers into new connections — one quick conversation a
 t a time. This lighthearted pre-show activity invites you to join our “s
 ocial” experiment and step out of your comfort zone into a few unexpecte
 d conversations. Inspired by our evening's speakers\, Dr. Nick Epley and D
 r. Gillian Sandstrom\, and in partnership with GenWell\, Canada's Human Co
 nnection Movement\, we're turning the simple act of talking to someone new
  into a game — equal parts curiosity\, fun\, and connection. No scripts\
 , no pressure — just a chance to discover how easy (and rewarding) it ca
 n be to connect with people you don't already know.\nYou'll leave with a f
 ew new acquaintances\, a fresh take on why talking to "strangers" isn’t 
 strange\, and a tool or two to keep connection going long after you leave 
 the library.\nInsights from this interactive workshop will be shared in\nS
 ay Hello to Connecting featuring Nick Epley and Gillian Sandstrom\n\, whic
 h follows at 7pm in the Appel Salon.\nYou can\nregister for that event her
 e\n.\nAbout this event's guests:\nGenWell\nis a Canadian charity on a miss
 ion to improve the nation's social health by inspiring more meaningful hum
 an connection. Through research\, storytelling\, workshops\, and hands-on 
 initiatives\, they help people rebuild the everyday habits — big and sma
 ll — that reduce feelings of loneliness\, disconnection\, and isolation.
 \n****\nThis interactive workshop is followed by\nHello to Connecting ft. 
 Nicholas Epley and Gillian Sandstorm\n\, which starts at 7pm in the Appel 
 Salon.\nYou can register for that event\nhere\n\, but please note if you w
 ish to attend the pre-event workshop you need to register separately\non t
 his page\n.\n***\nMake the most of your\nConnect IRL\nexperience by coming
  before or staying after the\nfeatured event\n. Grab a drink or snack at t
 he bar. Sign up for the workshop or try out one of the engagement activiti
 es available\, including this event's\nConversation Station: The\nBus Stop
  Challenge\n\, where you can take a moment or two to connect with a strang
 er in the most ordinary of small-talk settings.\nThe Bus Stop Challenge |\
 n5:30 – 7:00 pm & 8:00 – 9:00 pm\nConnect IRL\nis not your average ser
 ies of events\, workshops and activities\, but a real chance to connect wi
 th other Torontonians in meaningful and sometimes unexpected ways. Through
  conversation stations meant to spark one-on-one conversations\, or hands-
 on engagement activities and workshops before the featured event\, partici
 pants can explore the value of connection and community.\n***\nPLAN YOUR V
 ISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (
 789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 5:15pm\, Event starts at 
 approximately 5:30pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket polic
 y:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of people 
 have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 5:45pm or until ca
 pacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine av
 ailable for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committe
 d to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to
  request accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@
 tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be con
 tacted to fill out a brief survey following the program. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac69b53295b3b0033cadd08
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6ac8698e035faf0033db66c4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oi\nn a Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event
  series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid e
 mail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles
 .\nAttend all four sessions online via Zoom\, [date:]\nRegistration is a t
 wo-step procedure. First\, participants must complete their registration t
 hrough this page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to reques
 t additional information in order to complete the registration.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac8698e035faf0033db66c4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T203000
UID:6ac7b588686221156abba69e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\,\nThursdays Nov. 5\, 12\, 19 and 26 from 6-8:30pm.\nRegi
 stration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete their r
 egistration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow
  up to request additional information in order to complete the registratio
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7b588686221156abba69e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T190000
UID:6a97083f3b6c71003e5ceaf4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are 
 provided.\nWorkshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique – joi
 n in at any session and let’s write together!\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a97083f3b6c71003e5ceaf4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STOP on the Net Information Pop-Up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T160000
UID:6ac7dce5de300e00451920a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Thinking about quitting smoking? Join us on October 29 and Nov
 ember 19 from 12-4pm to learn more about\nSTOP on the Net\n\, a program th
 at provides free nicotine patches and gum/lozenges to help adults (18+) qu
 it smoking.\nStop by to speak with the team\, ask questions\, and learn ho
 w the program can help you achieve your goals.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Atrium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7dce5de300e00451920a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
