SUMMARY:How To Get the Most Out of the CRA's Website
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T130000
UID:6abc3761377296003a488614@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A representative from the\nCanada Revenue Agency (CRA)\nwill p
 rovide an overview of CRA's digital services\, including My Account\, a se
 cure portal that allows you to view your personal income tax and benefit i
 nformation and manage your tax affairs online. Learn how to register for a
 nd use My Account to track your refund\, view benefit and credit payments\
 , update personal information\, set up direct deposit\, receive online mai
 l\, and access a variety of CRA services.\nPresented as part of Financial 
 Literacy Month.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is free to join and wil
 l take place on\nZoom\n.\nRegister to receive an email with details on how
  to join the session. Join live\, as there will not be a recording for th
 is event.\nCaptions will be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining a
 nd participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc3761377296003a488614
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
